# ShellCheck configuration for the flac-health-reencode repo.
#
# Locating a sourced file and being allowed to FOLLOW it are separate settings;
# both are needed here:
#
#   source-path=tests
#       WHERE to look (like --source-path=tests). The cases source their shared
#       harness through a runtime variable -- `. "$TESTS_ROOT/helpers.sh"` -- which
#       ShellCheck cannot resolve alone, so it needs the directory. `tests` rather
#       than `.` because the cases are analysed as `tests/case_*.sh`, making their
#       relative path `./helpers.sh`.
#
#   external-sources=true
#       PERMISSION to read what was located (like -x). ShellCheck follows a source
#       only when the file is a command-line input or external sources are enabled.
#       The `lint` job analyses the test tree WITHOUT the production script in the
#       file list, so source_guard_units.sh sourcing ../flac_health_reencode.sh
#       raised SC1091 there while a combined local invocation passed and masked it.
#
# Safe: the only files sourced anywhere in the repo are helpers.sh and the
# production script, both trusted and tracked in-repo.
source-path=tests
external-sources=true